{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Origami to SwiftUI reference","role":"article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each Origami patch becomes in SwiftUI, so you know which construct — or which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" helper — to reach for."}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI both describe how values flow and change over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time, so the translations map onto SwiftUI’s own tools: computed properties for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pure math, gestures and "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for interaction, "},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for motion. Most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patches land on a native SwiftUI construct. A few need a helper from the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library, named after the patch it stands in for.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Patch → SwiftUI","type":"heading","anchor":"Patch-%E2%86%92-SwiftUI","level":2},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami patch"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, interpolate, logic)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression (native)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction (Tap, Press, Double Tap, Long Press)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/interaction(down:position:onTap:onDoubleTap:onLongPress:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — Drag","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Magnification \/ Pinch"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MagnifyGesture"},{"type":"text","text":" (native)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"origami.PopSwitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — Pop Switch"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" flipped on a threshold, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".spring"},{"text":" pop (native)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"builtin.layer.shape","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — Shape (triangle)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/RoundedTriangle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State \/ memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" + update logic (native)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop \/ Spring)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(.spring)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (native)","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body."}]},{"text":"How the categories map","type":"heading","anchor":"How-the-categories-map","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure value patches","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", interpolation, logic — carry no state. They run an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input through math and emit a result, which is exactly a computed property or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inline expression."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" exposes discrete outputs: "},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each becomes a SwiftUI gesture whose result lands in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"code":".interaction(…)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier attaches only the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recognizers you ask for, so gesture arbitration stays clean."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State and memory","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Switch"},{"type":"text","text":" — remember a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between evaluations. That is what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" is for; the update path is a gesture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback, an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"type":"text","text":", or an assignment."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — drives a value toward a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"target over time, which is a state change wrapped in "},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One naming note: Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" means ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"interpolation"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (mapping one range","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"onto another), not SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".transition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier for view insertion and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"removal.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"When a mapping isn’t exact","anchor":"When-a-mapping-isnt-exact","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics have no direct SwiftUI equivalent — continuous-time springs,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"custom JavaScript patches, absolute-position layout. Rather than approximate them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"silently, each translated view marks the gap with an inline "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TODO"},{"type":"text","text":" in its source,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the caveat travels with the code. The individual pattern pages link to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"source where those notes live."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami patterns, rebuilt as SwiftUI you can read — each one a worked example of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patches behind it, so you can see how a prototype’s behavior is written and reach for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same patch on your own layers."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami","title":"Swami","role":"collection"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/RoundedTriangle":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RoundedTriangle"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RoundedTriangle"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/RoundedTriangle","kind":"symbol","title":"RoundedTriangle","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/roundedtriangle","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An upward-pointing triangle with uniformly rounded corners."}],"type":"topic"}}}